# Next.js Fetch Architecture Rules
Version: 1.0

---

# Goal

Design every fetch in this project so that the application feels **instant**.

The user should never experience:

Loading page
↓

Skeleton
↓

Browser fetches API
↓

Content appears

Instead:

Request
↓

Server fetches everything
↓

HTML already contains data
↓

Instant paint

---

# Golden Rule

**If data is required to render the page, it MUST be fetched on the server.**

Never fetch page content inside:

- useEffect
- useLayoutEffect
- component mount
- SWR
- React Query

unless the feature explicitly requires live updates.

---

# Preferred Architecture

Browser

↓

Server Component

↓

API Layer

↓

Database / External API

NOT

Browser

↓

Client Component

↓

fetch()

↓

API

---

# Fetch Hierarchy

app/

layout.tsx
↓

page.tsx
↓

server helpers
↓

fetch()

↓

API

Client Components only receive props.

Client Components never own page data.

---

# Server Components

Every page should be:

```tsx
export default async function Page() {
    const data = await getData();

    return <PageView data={data} />;
}
```

Never:

```tsx
"use client";

useEffect(() => {
   fetch(...)
})
```

---

# API Layer

Never call fetch directly from pages.

Instead:

lib/

api/

cms.ts

users.ts

dashboard.ts

analytics.ts

Every endpoint should have a typed helper.

Example:

```ts
export async function getProjects() {}

export async function getUsers() {}

export async function getDashboard()
```

Pages should never know URLs.

---

# Native Fetch Only

Always prefer:

```ts
await fetch(...)
```

instead of Axios.

Reason:

Native fetch integrates with:

- Next Cache
- Revalidation
- Tags
- Streaming
- Server Components

---

# Cache Rules

Every fetch must intentionally choose one strategy.

Static content

```ts
next: {
   revalidate: 3600
}
```

Semi-dynamic

```ts
next: {
   revalidate: 300
}
```

Frequently changing

```ts
next: {
   revalidate: 30
}
```

Always fresh

```ts
cache: "no-store"
```

Never omit caching intentionally.

Every fetch must declare how it should behave.

---

# Parallel Fetching

Never:

```ts
const a = await getA();

const b = await getB();

const c = await getC();
```

Always:

```ts
const [a,b,c] = await Promise.all([
   getA(),
   getB(),
   getC()
]);
```

Sequential fetching is allowed ONLY when:

B depends on A.

---

# Global Data

Anything used across multiple pages belongs in layout.tsx.

Examples:

Navbar

Footer

Sidebar

User

Notifications

Settings

Workspace

Theme

Company

Do NOT fetch them repeatedly on every page.

---

# Client Components

Client Components exist only for:

Animations

Forms

Dropdowns

Dialogs

Tabs

Local State

Framer Motion

Input Handling

Drag & Drop

Realtime UI

They receive data.

They do not fetch page data.

---

# User Actions

Fetching after hydration is allowed ONLY for:

Submitting forms

Saving data

Deleting

Editing

Infinite scrolling

Realtime polling

WebSockets

Search autocomplete

Everything else belongs on the server.

